# inc-18q6 phase 5 (R19/R20). Walking onto a pool of slime must roll a real
# Reflex save, and the STUCK it grants must lapse on its own.
#
# THE DEFECT (both halves, before the fix). src/Move.cpp's sticky-terrain
# path (Creature::TerrainEffects) threw AD_STUK through the DAMAGE macro
# without ever setting saveDC, and EventInfo::Clear() memsets the struct, so
# it arrived as 0. Creature::SavingThrow (src/Creature.cpp) returns false --
# and prints NOTHING -- for DC <= 0: a zero DC is an automatic failure, not
# an automatic pass, and no "Reflex Save:" line was ever possible for this
# hazard. The same call passed -1 as the duration, and
# Thing::UpdateStati (src/Status.cpp) only ever decrements a Duration
# greater than zero, so the STUCK it granted never expired.
#
# THE ORACLE, half one (R19). A DC above zero means SavingThrow actually
# rolls and prints. "Reflex Save: ... vs DC 15 [failure]." on the turn the
# character gets stuck is impossible on the unfixed tree -- it would print
# nothing at all -- so its mere appearance is the assertion.
#
# THE ORACLE, half two (R20), and why it does NOT look like escaping. Pool
# of slime's own hazard check re-runs every turn a creature stands on it
# (the only guard is "not already Stuck"), so a creature who does nothing
# but wait is caught again the instant the old grant expires -- correctly:
# he is still standing in the puddle. That makes "still Stuck" on the status
# line USELESS as a signal by itself; a permanently-stuck creature and a
# finite one that keeps getting re-caught both show it forever. The signal
# this script uses instead: the printed roll line is DIFFERENT after a long
# wait than it was right after the first catch. A different 1d20 result (and,
# once ENTANGLED's -4 Dexterity joins in, a different modifier) can only mean
# a SECOND roll happened -- which requires the FIRST grant to have expired,
# which requires a finite Duration. Measured at seed 4 with this exact
# fixture: the fourth roll after getting stuck (100 waits later) reads
# "Reflex Save: 1d20 (2) +1 base = 3 vs DC 15 [failure]", not the "1d20 (6)
# +3 base = 9" the character got stuck on. On the unfixed tree (Duration -1)
# that line would never change no matter how long the wait runs, because the
# original grant is permanent and the guard blocks any second roll.
#
# THE GUARD, so a change to the ESCAPE mechanic cannot fake this pass: no
# "Escape Artist Check:", "Strength Check:", "You tear free!" or "You remain
# stuck fast!" may appear anywhere in this script's output. Every key this
# fixture sends after getting stuck is "." (Wait One Turn) -- nothing here
# ever tries to move or escape, so none of those lines has any legitimate
# way to appear. If one does, the difference proved above came from the
# escape mechanic, not from Duration, and the check must not pass.
#
# The subject and setup mirror tools/keys/entangle-strength-escape.keys and
# tools/keys/entangled-acts.keys: the seed-4 human paladin, wizard mode with
# monsters frozen, and the wizard terrain-paint command ([X], page 1 of
# "Which terrain type?", no TAB) instead of tanglefoot's [j] on page 2. Two
# squares are painted, as tanglefoot's fixtures do, because the first
# attempt at this hazard on this seed rolls Reflex successfully (no stuck,
# nothing to measure) and only the second fails.
#
# Usage: tools/check_sticky_save.sh   (0 pass, 1 fail, 2 inconclusive)

@include chargen-paladin.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC
w
K
RIGHT
ENTER
X
w
K
RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
X
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:try1
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:got-stuck
.*25
@dump:wait25
.*25
@dump:wait50
.*25
@dump:wait75
.*25
@dump:wait100
@quit
